<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pakubuwana III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1732">1732</a>–<a href="/years/1788">1788</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pakubuwana III was ruler of Mataram from 1749 and the first susuhunan of Surakarta, installed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>. His uncle Mangkubumi contested the throne, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-giyanti">Treaty of Giyanti</a> of 1755 divided the realm between them, leaving Pakubuwana III at Surakarta. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-salatiga">Treaty of Salatiga</a> of 1757 split off a further principality, Mangkunegaran.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakubuwana-iii.jpg" alt="Pakubuwana III" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pakubuwana_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
